      "widgets_values": [
        "{\"version\":1,\"content\":\"<h1>RUN TIMES</h1><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Measured on a <b>24 GB RTX 4090</b> with this workflow, with the models already loaded. A different card gives different numbers, but the shape holds: the time grows with the number of pictures and their size.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><table class=\\\"pix-note-grid\\\" style=\\\"--pix-note-grid-border: #f66744; --pix-note-grid-header-bg: #1a1a1a\\\"><thead><tr><th>What</th><th>Time</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>6 pictures, 1024 to 2048 (the demo)</td><td>about 24 s</td></tr><tr><td>Each 1024 picture you add</td><td>about 4 s more</td></tr></tbody></table><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Measured on an RTX 4090, model loading included. Bigger pictures take longer: the time grows with the number of pixels. The model is small, so slower cards work too, only slower.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"warning-v1\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;The first Run of the session</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>The first Run after starting ComfyUI also has to load the models from disk (about 18 GB for Klein and its text encoder), so it takes longer. After that they stay loaded.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"run-timer\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;On a 16 GB card</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Timed on an <b>RTX 4060 Ti 16 GB</b> with 32 GB of RAM:</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li>The upscale took about <b>2.5 times</b> as long.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p>\",\"buttonColor\":\"#f66744\",\"lineColor\":\"#f66744\",\"backgroundColor\":\"#2a2a2a\",\"info\":{\"title\":\"Run Times\",\"icon\":\"run-timer\",\"color\":\"#3f9a4f\"}}"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "note_json": "{\"version\":1,\"content\":\"<h1>RUN TIMES</h1><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Measured on a <b>24 GB RTX 4090</b> with this workflow, with the models already loaded. A different card gives different numbers, but the shape holds: the time grows with the number of pictures and their size.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><table class=\\\"pix-note-grid\\\" style=\\\"--pix-note-grid-border: #f66744; --pix-note-grid-header-bg: #1a1a1a\\\"><thead><tr><th>What</th><th>Time</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>6 pictures, 1024 to 2048 (the demo)</td><td>about 24 s</td></tr><tr><td>Each 1024 picture you add</td><td>about 4 s more</td></tr></tbody></table><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Measured on an RTX 4090, model loading included. Bigger pictures take longer: the time grows with the number of pixels. The model is small, so slower cards work too, only slower.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"warning-v1\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;The first Run of the session</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>The first Run after starting ComfyUI also has to load the models from disk (about 18 GB for Klein and its text encoder), so it takes longer. After that they stay loaded.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"run-timer\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;On a 16 GB card</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Timed on an <b>RTX 4060 Ti 16 GB</b> with 32 GB of RAM:</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li>The upscale took about <b>2.5 times</b> as long.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p>\",\"buttonColor\":\"#f66744\",\"lineColor\":\"#f66744\",\"backgroundColor\":\"#2a2a2a\",\"info\":{\"title\":\"Run Times\",\"icon\":\"run-timer\",\"color\":\"#3f9a4f\"}}"
